<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-panama"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Panama.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Panama</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Flag riots in the Canal Zone leave more than 20 Panamanians dead</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bunyoro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bunyoro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A referendum returns two 'lost counties' from Buganda to Bunyoro</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/barotseland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Barotseland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Barotseland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Barotseland Agreement brings the kingdom into independent Zambia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sultanate%20of%20Zanzibar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sultanate of Zanzibar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Zanzibar Revolution overthrows the sultan; union with Tanganyika follows</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20South%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of South Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nelson Mandela is sentenced to life imprisonment at the end of the Rivonia Trial</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tanzania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tanzania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tanzania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tanganyika and Zanzibar unite on 26 April; the name Tanzania is adopted in October</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/anti-apartheid-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anti-apartheid%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anti-apartheid movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nelson Mandela and seven others are sentenced to life imprisonment in the Rivonia Trial</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/civil-rights-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Civil%20rights%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Civil rights movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Civil Rights Act outlaws segregation in public places and discrimination in employment</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/hoabinhian"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hoabinhian.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hoabinhian</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">J. M. Matthews shows that the cobble tools of Sai Yok form a continuous range rather than Colani’s distinct types</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/liberalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Liberalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liberalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Civil Rights Act passes in the United States, part of the rapid series of reforms some historians call the Liberal Hour</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/hindutva"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hindutva.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hindutva</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Vishva Hindu Parishad is founded to protect and promote the Hindu religion</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/nelson-mandela"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nelson%20Mandela.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nelson Mandela</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">At the Rivonia Trial he is found guilty of sabotage and conspiracy and sentenced to life imprisonment</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/northern-rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Northern%20Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Northern Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 24 October the country becomes independent as the Republic of Zambia, with Kaunda as President</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/jawaharlal-nehru"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jawaharlal%20Nehru.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jawaharlal Nehru</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nehru dies in office and is succeeded by Lal Bahadur Shastri</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/kwame-nkrumah"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kwame%20Nkrumah.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kwame Nkrumah</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A constitutional amendment makes Ghana a one-party state with Nkrumah as president for life</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/martin-luther-king-jr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr..png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Martin Luther King Jr.</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Becomes the youngest winner of the Nobel Peace Prize; the Civil Rights Act is passed</span></li></ul></section>
